# Changelog
## [0.2.1] - 2026-08-25
### New features
 - Added AmneziaWG 3.1 device attributes: `RandomTrailers` and
   `DisableCookies` (`u8` flags, attribute kinds 33 and 34). Only the
   AmneziaWG 3.1+ kernel module accepts them; the genl family version is
   still 3.

## [0.1.2] - 2026-06-06
### Breaking changes
 - Changed `H1`..`H4` and `I1`..`I5` attribute types from `u16` to `String`
   to match the AmneziaWG kernel module (`NLA_NUL_STRING`).
 - Removed unsupported `DataInit`, `DataResponse`, `DataConfirm`, and
   `DataTransport` attributes (they are not present in the kernel module).

### Bug fixes
 - `SetDevice` with magic header specs no longer returns `EINVAL`.

## [0.1.1] - 2026-06-06
### Breaking changes
 - Dropped generic `WgFamily` trait; the crate is now AmneziaWG-only.
 - Renamed all public types from `Wireguard*` to `AmneziaWireguard*` to avoid
   name collisions with the plain WireGuard crate.
 - Merged `AmneziaWgAttribute` into `WireguardAttribute` (now the single
   attribute enum containing both base and Amnezia-specific fields).
 - Family name hard-coded to `"amneziawg"` and version to `2`.

### New features
 - Added AmneziaWG-specific attributes: `JC`, `Jmin`, `Jmax`, `S1`..`S4`,
   `H1`..`H4`, `I1`..`I5`, `DataInit`, `DataResponse`, `DataConfirm`,
   `DataTransport`.
 - Exposed `pub mod constants` with kernel flags.
 - Added 7 new unit tests and 3 integration tests for Linux.
 - Added GitHub Actions CI with AmneziaWG kernel module.

### Bug fixes
 - Fixed clippy warnings (needless borrow, op_ref, await_holding_lock).

## [0.1.0] - 2026-06-06
### Breaking changes
 - Forked from `netlink-packet-wireguard` to support AmneziaWG.

### New features
 - Generic netlink packet definitions for Amnezia WireGuard.

## [0.3.0] - 2026-01-26
### Breaking changes
 - Rewrite to align with netlink-packet-route code style. (3067a39)
     - All netlink attribute are marked as `#[non_exhaustive]`.
     - Renamed `Wireguard` to `WireguardMessage`.
     - Renamed `WgDeviceAttrs` to `WireguardAttribute`.
     - Renamed `WgAllowedIp` to `WireguardAllowedIp`.
     - Renamed `WgPeerAttrs` to `WireguardPeer`.
     - Renamed `WgPeer` to `WireguardPeerAttribute`.
     - Will not expose any constants.
     - Changed the use of `std::time::SystemTime` to self-defined
       `WireguardTimeSpec`.
     - Do not raise error for unknown attribute but store in
       `Self::Other(DefaultNla)`.

### New features
 - N/A

### Bug fixes
 - N/A

